\section{Counting}{

Each plan-county appears once, so sums count every enrollee once. The
share of December enrollment in plans CMS terminated or cut from the
county is
\code{sum(dec_enrollment[exit_type != "none"]) / sum(dec_enrollment)}, and
\code{exit_type} splits it into terminations and service-area reductions.
}

\section{December and September}{

December enrollment covers the transitions in \code{MAEXITS_XWALK_YEARS}.
September covers \code{MAEXITS_EXITS_YEARS}, which adds the newest
transition once its crosswalk is registered, two months before its
December enrollment comes out: compare it with earlier years through
\code{sep_enrollment}.
September gives shares 0.01-0.28 points higher than December
(2018-2025). The plan-counties and \code{exit_type} are the same for both
months.
}

\section{What counts as an exit}{

\code{exit_type} uses only CMS's crosswalk labels, checked against the
January landscape for the county: \code{terminated} when every crosswalk link
of the plan-county is a termination, \code{service_area_reduction} when the
plan renews with a service-area reduction and no plan it maps to serves
the county. \link{displacement} also counts as lost coverage the
plan-counties CMS moved to a plan that does not serve the county (by
consolidation or a New Plan link), or renewed without listing in the
county in January (together 0.03-0.31\% of December enrollment a year);
here they are \code{none}.
}

